« Pet Rescue Saga Level 26 Help
- More missions , challenges , and surprises !
If you are stuck on the Pet Rescue Saga Facebook game and looking for help on how to pass, how to solve, and how to beat Pet Rescue Saga then you have come to the right place.
The good news is there are some strategies available to try and crunch your way through some tougher times.
Some blocks are in cages, these can be freed by destroying adjacent blocks …but not by balloons!
or is a case of by any means possible?
There are quite a few different elements in this game and figuring out how to capitalize on each one effectively is important!
Balloons do not need to be matched with any other bricks and can be handy to clear a board with few possible matches, just keep in mind if you blow them up with a bomb they won’t work.
Cages – Some levels have bricks in cages, you have to hit these with an adjacent match to free the bricks to enable them to be destroyed.
Bombs – these little black beauties do what bombs do best..they go boom!
Note you can set off a bomb next to a pet quite safely, they really dont seem to mind!
Freed bombs can be saved until a pet is just above it.
– you know how you get the urge to lock up a rock?
well someone at King does, anyway the keys are hidden on the board, generally in a glass case that needs to be smashed open by either dropping to the ground or onto a solid rock, pipe, bit of earth or other random feature (not onto another glass box though) once the key is freed you dont have to use it immediately, it will hang around until you need to use it.
Double ended spring– this little piece of geniusness once activated clears an entire line horizontally in both directions, they are particularly useful when faced with metal boxes!
just an extra added speed bump I guess.
Match two or more blocks of the same color to clear the level and save the pets from the evil Pet Snatchers!
