How to store glue in winter?
Why is there a white glue line at the splicing part of the board?
When splicing wood has defects in processing accuracy, the glue line formed by filling the defective parts with the splicing glue.
When the pressure of the jigsaw machine is insufficient or uneven, the glue of the jigsaw can be fully squeezed out of the rubber particles or glue lines, and a white glue line with glue retention is formed.
Gluing time is too long or the open time after gluing is too long, causing the glue line problem caused by the false adhesion formed by the formation of the glue layer.
The white glue line formed by the overtime use of the jigsaw glue or the low temperature of the jigsaw wood will cause the glue to condense and penetrate poorly, and the glue layer stays.
The moisture content is 8-12%. The moisture content error of adjacent wood on the same panel is not more than +/- 1%, and the deviation of wood moisture content on the same panel is not more than +/- 2%.
The particularity of wood (anisotropy) The shrinkage/expansion rate in different directions is different, and the stress produced is different.
The bonding of substrates with different moisture content will cause the height difference of the interface (the ends of the assembled boards are prone to cracking)
The wood gluing surface should be flat, smooth, oil-free, and not curved; the adjacent two sides of the wood jigsaw glue should be at right angles; the processing error of the wood gluing surface should not be greater than 0.1mm; keep the wood gluing surface fresh. The processed substrate can be assembled within 24 hours.
Why should the glue be stirred well?
