In addition to knowing the profile of the applicants, they apply emotional intelligence test, general intelligence tests and some other instrument that is considered necessary for employment, even they are also applied in children and adolescents
At Grand Hotelier in addition to being interested in the candidate's education, skills, experience and cognitive abilities, another key indicator of success in the workplace is considered: emotional intelligence.
Emotional intelligence is a long process for a person to develop through training. To find out more, be sure to read this article.
1.1 What is emotional intelligence?
1.7 4 Key Benefits of Personality Tests
Tests and Emotional Intelligence Tests can be an overall success factor in any workplace. Commonly known as EI, emotional intelligence is the ability of a person to identify, evaluate and manage personal feelings and those of other people, as individuals or as groups.
1- Emotional awareness
Conscious people can recognize the relationship between what they feel and the way they behave.
Likewise, being aware of your emotions and the impact they can have on you and others requires you to be able to regulate and manage your emotions.
People with good self-control skills tend to be flexible, adapt well to change, and are also able to handle conflict and relieve tension.
In addition, knowing how to handle your own emotions also means developing a more positive approach to life. Being able to regulate your emotional state is essential and can save you from impulsive behavior that you may regret in the future.
3- Motivate yourself and others
In fact, another very important skill, especially when working in a group, is knowing how to influence and inspire others. Motivating people is an art and it's a bit like selling ideas, using the best persuasion techniques.
In fact, this state comes when you are completely immersed in a task that you like to do, you are focused on the goal, and your emotional state is absolutely positive.
Ultimately, being empathetic enables people to understand the power dynamics that often influence social relationships, teamwork, problem solving, and decision-making, especially in the workplace.
In the workplace, knowing how to build quality relationships with colleagues is important both in working well on the team and in leadership to influence and inspire others.
At Grand Hotelier we consider that successful people are those who have good emotional intelligence. If you are a person who knows how to handle your anxieties, deal with difficult situations, the ability to relate, work as a team and get up again, you have strong potential that can guarantee you a successful future.
