Learn to Select your Airplane Seats in Volaris according to your Preferences
Some of us fall asleep before the plane takes off, and others travel with children or fight with long legs. That is why we will tell you how to choose the best seat according to the type of passenger you are, and your preferences.
The Best Airplane Seat for a Peaceful Travel
If so, you've likely experienced the horror of waking up mid-flight to the realization that you are drooling at the friendly passenger next to you.
If you want to fall asleep, choose a window seat near the front, and preferably on the left side of the plane.
Why are the Front and Left Side Airplane Seats the best?
We know the difficulties involved in carrying long legs for these flights. This is why you should try to get a seat in the emergency exit row, preferably an aisle seat.
If you are flying a Volaris aircraft with two aisles, choose a seat in the front with aisle access on the left. The boarding gate of the plane is always on the left, so the aisle tends to move faster than the aisle on the right side.
The Seat Indicated for Traveling with Children
When traveling with children, try to get a line behind a wall. These rows offer extra space in the front, so children can stand up a time , and to prevent them from moving from time to time.
Seats of this type are also usually close to the toilets, making last-minute emergencies with children a bit easier.
The window is a healthy distraction for children and, more importantly, it prevents them from being run over by drink carts, by passengers running to the bathroom, or from falling into the hallway.
