2 What is the Landing Gear of an Airplane
It is designed to support the aircraft's load during surface operations.
When the third wheel is on the nose, it is called a nose wheel and the design is known as a tricycle gear.
You can read: The PARTS of an AIRPLANE
There are several types of landing gear that fall into four main categories:
You will be interested in: REQUIREMENTS to have a JOB as an AVIATOR PILOT
Allows adequate ground clearance for a larger propeller
If the pilot allows the aircraft to roll while rolling on the ground at low speed, they may not have enough rudder control and the center of gravity will try to get ahead of the main gear, which can cause the aircraft to roll toward the ground. .
Airplanes with tricycle landing gear have two main wheels attached to the fuselage behind their center of gravity, these bear most of the weight of the structure.
Allows better forward visibility for the pilot during takeoff, landing and taxiing.
In fact, some types of tricycle gear are very capable and versatile.
