Through this article, we will show you how important the life jacket is, for your safety and that of yours.
Although the price can vary depending on the brands, from $ 250 to $ 1,500 or more, however there are used life jackets for sale, which in good condition, if you do not have the budget, it will be worth acquiring them to risk not using one.
People since ancient times have always looked for a way to float on water; for this they have used: animal skins, some parts of wooden boats or different pieces made of cork; among others.
These disasters have caused the manufacture and design of life jackets to be perfected and increased.
It can be hard to imagine how something so light can keep a person afloat.
It tells us that when an object is submerged in water, it moves or moves in the water according to its weight. Archimedes found that the water will exert an upward push against the object with a force equal to the weight of the moving water.
A bowling ball and a beach ball may have the same volume, but the bowling ball weighs much more and is much denser than the beach ball.
The beach ball, meanwhile, displaces very little water, and the air inside it is much lighter than the weight of the water that was displaced. The buoyant force from below keeps the beach ball afloat.
Enjoy this Article: The most BEAUTIFUL BEACHES in MEXICO, a delight!
Buoyancy is the upward force we need from the water to keep us above the surface, and it is measured by weight.
Our bodies are mostly water, so the density of a person is quite close to that of water, because of this, an average person needs only seven to 12 pounds of additional buoyancy to float. A life jacket provides this additional lift.
The Material of the Life Jacket The outside of a lifejacket is almost always made of nylon or vinyl, and the material inside a lifejacket traps air when the lifejacket is submerged.
On the market you can find life-saving floats that inflate, thanks to a carbon dioxide gas capsule that is attached to the same vest. The mechanism of action is simple, once it is executed, the gas is released and it will fill the entire internal space of the vest.
For the proper use and operation of the life jacket you must take into account the following:
All passengers on a boat, boat or any water transport, must properly put on life jackets and use them whenever they are near bodies of water.
Children's floats such as wings, toys, rafts, and inflatable mattresses, they should never be used to replace life jackets. These do not provide the necessary security.
Knowing how a life jacket works and knowing the importance of its use will help you enjoy pleasant and safe trips.
